1
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,410
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:51,670 --> 00:01:55,010
Is he going to skip school again?

37
00:01:55,970 --> 00:01:57,970
Little Shin's Room

38
00:01:58,890 --> 00:02:02,810
Shinji, wake up! How long are you going
to keep skipping school?

39
00:02:02,810 --> 00:02:06,310
It's been five days now. Unit 01 has
already been completely repaired.

40
00:02:06,310 --> 00:02:09,150
So don't you think the pilot needs
to get his act together too?

41
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:10,440
Shinji?!

42
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:21,910
Miss Misato Katsuragi

43
00:02:27,870 --> 00:02:30,670
He's run away.
I suppose that's not surprising.

44
00:02:30,710 --> 00:02:35,170
EPISODE 04
RAIN, AFTER RUNNING AWAY

45
00:02:42,470 --> 00:02:43,550
Shinji?

46
00:02:44,390 --> 00:02:46,020
Well...

47
00:02:48,430 --> 00:02:52,110
We're Ikari's classmates,
Aida and Suzuhara, Ma'am.

48
00:02:52,110 --> 00:02:54,020
Aida and Suzuhara?

49
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:54,690
Yes, Ma'am!

50
00:02:54,690 --> 00:02:56,730
I'm Suzuhara.

51
00:02:57,650 --> 00:03:00,570
Aren't you the boys who got in
Unit 01's entry plug?

52
00:03:00,570 --> 00:03:01,200
Yes, Ma'am!

53
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:03,700
We're sorry for causing so much trouble.

54
00:03:04,530 --> 00:03:08,250
Actually, Ikari's been absent ever since then,

55
00:03:08,250 --> 00:03:10,710
so we came to see if he was okay.

56
00:03:10,710 --> 00:03:14,420
He's at the Nerv training facility right now.

57
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:16,090
Oh, I see.

58
00:03:16,090 --> 00:03:19,800
These are the printouts that were
building up on Ikari's desk.

59
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:22,390
Oh, sorry for your trouble. Thank you.

60
00:03:22,390 --> 00:03:24,600
Well, we'll be leaving now.

61
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:26,930
Please say "hi" to Ikari for us.

62
00:03:26,930 --> 00:03:29,730
Yeah, I will. Bye.

63
00:03:35,730 --> 00:03:38,320
This is an unexpected development.

64
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:40,450
She was a real babe, wasn't she?

65
00:03:43,870 --> 00:03:45,580
Shinji, you idiot!

66
00:03:49,750 --> 00:03:51,000
Idiot!

67
00:03:56,750 --> 00:04:00,380
<i><i>The next station is
Nagao Toge, Nagao Toge.</i></i>

68
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:02,930
<i><i>The exit will switch to the right side.</i></i>

69
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:08,370
<i><i>Thank you for using New Tokyo-3
Loop Seven.</i></i>

70
00:05:08,370 --> 00:05:11,740
<i><i>This train will be going out of service
at this station.</i></i>

71
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:16,170
<i><i>Please, make sure you take all of your
belongings as you exit the train.</i></i>

72
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:23,340
I've got to go back.

73
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:26,930
<i>Hey there! We're offering you
a great bargain!</i>

74
00:05:26,930 --> 00:05:29,140
<i>Hot young babes serving
heavenly refreshment!</i>

75
00:05:29,140 --> 00:05:32,970
<i>Special services to heal your tired body,
services to fill you with energy!</i>

76
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:36,850
<i>You really couldn't detect it, Doctor?!!</i>

77
00:05:36,850 --> 00:05:39,520
<i>Yes. An object only ten
millimeters in diameter</i>

78
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:43,070
<i>crashed into Antarctica at close
to the speed of light.</i>

79
00:05:43,070 --> 00:05:46,450
<i>The technology we had was unable
to predict or prevent such a thing.</i>

80
00:05:46,450 --> 00:05:49,240
<i>It's like hell out there! Just what is
the purpose of science?!</i>

81
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:53,200
<i>The atmospheric flux caused by the
change in the Earth's axis</i>

82
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:55,160
<i>has decreased by 3%.</i>

83
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:57,330
<i>So it's getting a little better?</i>

84
00:05:57,330 --> 00:06:00,750
<i>No, there's still a tidal wave approaching
at 230 meters a second!</i>

85
00:06:00,750 --> 00:06:02,380
<i>Doctor! We must evacuate!</i>

86
00:06:02,380 --> 00:06:05,090
<i>It's my duty to remain here.</i>

87
00:06:05,090 --> 00:06:07,090
<i>Doctor, choosing death is easy,</i>

88
00:06:07,090 --> 00:06:10,050
<i>but you have an obligation
to watch this living hell!</i>

89
00:06:16,930 --> 00:06:25,900
Documentary!
The World Sinks...
Second Impact
Tokyo-2
Tokyo

90
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:23,750
Idiot.

91
00:07:27,670 --> 00:07:30,630
Arrival Stop Only

92
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:18,760
He's only fourteen years old.

93
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:23,480
It seems so cruel, making him bear
the burden of mankind's destiny.

94
00:08:23,850 --> 00:08:29,820
But we have no choice but to entrust the
piloting of the Evas to fourteen year olds.

95
00:08:30,070 --> 00:08:31,530
I know.

96
00:08:31,530 --> 00:08:34,070
So, has he called?

97
00:08:35,530 --> 00:08:36,740
No?

98
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:42,910
No. I think he might never come back.

99
00:08:43,620 --> 00:08:45,370
What are you going to do?

100
00:08:45,370 --> 00:08:47,000
Nothing really.

101
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,300
If he won't come back,
maybe that's for the better.

102
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:50,800
Why?

103
00:08:51,710 --> 00:08:54,340
After the battle the other day...

104
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:58,350
Why did you ignore my order?

105
00:08:59,260 --> 00:09:00,720
I'm sorry.

106
00:09:01,140 --> 00:09:04,060
I'm the one who's in charge
of your operations, right?

107
00:09:04,060 --> 00:09:04,770
Yes.

108
00:09:04,770 --> 00:09:08,900
You have a duty to obey my orders.
Do you understand?

109
00:09:08,900 --> 00:09:09,820
Yes.

110
00:09:09,820 --> 00:09:11,900
I'm warning you, never do it again.

111
00:09:11,900 --> 00:09:12,570
Yes.

112
00:09:12,570 --> 00:09:15,070
Do you really understand what I'm saying?!

113
00:09:15,070 --> 00:09:16,110
Yes.

114
00:09:16,110 --> 00:09:20,830
Hey, you're not going to get out of this
by just saying yes to everything I say.

115
00:09:20,830 --> 00:09:25,250
I know that. That's enough, isn't it?
We won the battle anyway.

116
00:09:26,370 --> 00:09:30,340
You know, it may seem easy to go along
with whatever anyone else wants,

117
00:09:30,340 --> 00:09:33,260
but if you get into the Eva with that attitude,
it'll kill you!

118
00:09:33,260 --> 00:09:35,670
I don't care.

119
00:09:36,260 --> 00:09:38,970
It'd be nice if I could say you've got
the right attitude,

120
00:09:38,970 --> 00:09:42,600
but if you expect to get any praise out of me,
you're wrong, Shinji Ikari.

121
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:46,690
That's not the point. In any case, I'm the
only one who can pilot it, aren't I?

122
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:49,360
I'll do it.

123
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:51,480
I see.

124
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:58,360
If piloting an Eva means nothing
but pain to him,

125
00:09:58,360 --> 00:10:00,030
he shouldn't get into it again.

126
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,790
Otherwise, I'm sure he'll get killed.

127
00:10:02,790 --> 00:10:04,870
But we need pilots.

128
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:14,090
Captain!

129
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:16,800
Aida, go on ahead!

130
00:10:17,420 --> 00:10:21,930
But I can't go and leave you behind!

131
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:23,970
You fool!

132
00:10:34,150 --> 00:10:35,860
Upsy-daisy.

133
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:42,410
The new kid?

134
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,160
Ikari!

135
00:11:00,550 --> 00:11:02,970
Summer Training Drill Operation Outline
Today's Scheduled Operations
15:00 Deploy for Combat
16:00 Prepare for Attack,
Commence Firing

136
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:05,060
Toji was sorry about that.

137
00:11:05,060 --> 00:11:07,770
He said that his kid sister scolded him

138
00:11:07,770 --> 00:11:11,350
and said that, "It was the robot
who saved our lives!"

139
00:11:11,770 --> 00:11:15,730
That's pretty embarrassing, being
chewed out by a grade school kid.

140
00:11:16,230 --> 00:11:17,030
Right?

141
00:11:21,490 --> 00:11:25,490
I like it at night because those
noisy cicadas don't chirp.

142
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:28,410
Although I remember that it was pretty quiet
when I was a kid,

143
00:11:28,410 --> 00:11:30,580
there've been more of them each year.

144
00:11:30,580 --> 00:11:33,040
The ecosystem is returning
to its former state.

145
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:34,290
That's what Miss Misato said.

146
00:11:35,790 --> 00:11:37,550
I see, Miss Misato said so.

147
00:11:37,550 --> 00:11:39,420
I really envy you.

148
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:43,840
Living with such a beautiful woman
and piloting the Evangelion.

149
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:48,850
I wish I could get behind
the controls just once!

150
00:11:49,310 --> 00:11:52,770
You shouldn't. I think your mother
would be worried.

151
00:11:54,270 --> 00:11:57,940
Oh, don't worry about that. I don't have one.

152
00:12:00,030 --> 00:12:01,530
I'm the same as you.

153
00:12:04,110 --> 00:12:06,280
You'll have something to eat, won't you?

154
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:07,370
Yeah.

155
00:12:08,450 --> 00:12:10,500
Do you usually do this sort of thing?

156
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:13,250
Huh? Well, sure.

157
00:12:13,540 --> 00:12:17,090
Is this some kind of training for
guerilla warfare or something?

158
00:12:17,090 --> 00:12:21,010
How could I fight with toys like these?
It's just for fun.

159
00:12:45,950 --> 00:12:48,620
You're Shinji Ikari, aren't you?

160
00:12:48,620 --> 00:12:49,790
Yes.

161
00:12:49,790 --> 00:12:52,410
We're from Nerv Security Intelligence.

162
00:12:52,410 --> 00:12:57,210
Under Article 8 of the Security Act,
we're taking you to headquarters.

163
00:12:57,580 --> 00:12:58,960
All right?

164
00:12:58,960 --> 00:12:59,420
Yes.

165
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:06,760
And all you did was stand there?

166
00:13:07,090 --> 00:13:08,510
That's easy for you to say!

167
00:13:08,510 --> 00:13:11,720
But it's like I said, they were Nerv
Security Intelligence, professionals.

168
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:16,440
So what?! Don't you have any balls at all?!

169
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:17,190
Sissy!

170
00:13:17,190 --> 00:13:17,900
Pervert!

171
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:18,520
Ape!

172
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:21,280
Only an idiot fights when
he knows he can't win.

173
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:22,900
Balls have nothing to do with it.

174
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:36,460
Long time, no see.

175
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:37,420
Yes.

176
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:40,840
Do you feel any better after wandering
around for two days?

177
00:13:41,380 --> 00:13:42,760
I don't know.

178
00:13:43,090 --> 00:13:46,090
The Eva is on standby. Will you pilot it?

179
00:13:47,130 --> 00:13:48,510
Or won't you?

180
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:52,510
You're not going to scold me
for running away?

181
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:59,100
Of course not. I'm not related to you, am I?

182
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:04,530
If I say that I won't pilot Unit 01,
what will you do with it?

183
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:06,990
I suppose that Rei will do it.

184
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,450
Won't you pilot it?

185
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:15,410
It seems unrealistic for you
to force everything on her.

186
00:14:15,410 --> 00:14:18,120
Don't worry. I'll pilot it.

187
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:19,830
But you don't want to do it?

188
00:14:19,830 --> 00:14:23,960
Of course not. To begin with, it's not
something that comes to me naturally.

189
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:27,380
But Ayanami, Miss Misato and Miss Ritsuko...

190
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:29,220
Cut that out!

191
00:14:29,220 --> 00:14:31,300
This has nothing to do with any of us!

192
00:14:31,300 --> 00:14:33,260
If you don't like it, get out of here!

193
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:37,310
Just forget all about Eva and us and
go back to where you came from!

194
00:14:38,850 --> 00:14:42,270
We don't need someone
with that attitude piloting!

195
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:57,290
The Third Child is leaving
New Tokyo-3 tomorrow.

196
00:14:57,290 --> 00:15:00,250
Then we'll reconfigure
Unit 01's system for Rei.

197
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:01,500
But...

198
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:04,670
Regardless of the results of Unit 00's
re-activation experiments,

199
00:15:04,670 --> 00:15:06,920
we'll move on to experimenting with Unit 01.

200
00:15:12,050 --> 00:15:14,640
According to the Marduk
Organization's report,

201
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:17,470
the Fourth Child hasn't been found yet.

202
00:15:17,470 --> 00:15:20,350
That means we can't get
any pilot replacements?

203
00:15:23,230 --> 00:15:27,730
Excuse me, where is Miss Misato?
I'd like to say goodbye.

204
00:15:27,730 --> 00:15:30,650
You're no longer Nerv personnel.

205
00:15:30,650 --> 00:15:33,120
Therefore, we can't give you any information.

206
00:15:46,750 --> 00:15:47,880
Ikari!

207
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:49,050
You forgot this!

208
00:15:58,930 --> 00:16:01,520
Could you excuse me for a moment?

209
00:16:04,610 --> 00:16:07,110
Thank you.

210
00:16:09,070 --> 00:16:10,400
Hey, Toji.

211
00:16:10,400 --> 00:16:11,950
Come on, say something!

212
00:16:14,450 --> 00:16:19,370
Ikari, I'm sorry I hit you twice.
Please, hit me back!

213
00:16:19,370 --> 00:16:21,000
I can't do that.

214
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,710
Please! Otherwise, I won't be satisfied.

215
00:16:23,710 --> 00:16:26,080
See? He's a pretty embarrassing guy,
isn't he?

216
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:28,460
But if it'll put an end to this dispute,
why don't you go ahead and hit him?

217
00:16:30,050 --> 00:16:31,010
But...

218
00:16:31,010 --> 00:16:33,630
Hurry up! You don't have
much time, do you?

219
00:16:34,010 --> 00:16:36,550
Okay, but only once.

220
00:16:36,550 --> 00:16:38,220
Okay! Come on!

221
00:16:42,270 --> 00:16:43,600
Hold it!

222
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:47,190
No holdin' back.

223
00:16:47,190 --> 00:16:48,230
Right.

224
00:16:51,070 --> 00:16:51,860
Ouch...

225
00:17:03,410 --> 00:17:04,750
How did you know I'd be here?

226
00:17:04,750 --> 00:17:10,210
Call it a hunch. We've seen
dozens of classmates off now.

227
00:17:12,840 --> 00:17:18,430
If you're leavin', we'll have to leave
this city sometime soon,

228
00:17:18,430 --> 00:17:25,480
but we can't blame you for that.
We saw how you suffered in the Eva.

229
00:17:25,850 --> 00:17:28,810
And if anyone tries to blame you,

230
00:17:29,650 --> 00:17:31,280
I'm gonna give them a head butt!

231
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:37,990
Hey, don't look so gloomy.

232
00:17:37,990 --> 00:17:39,320
Take care.

233
00:17:39,320 --> 00:17:40,490
Good luck!

234
00:17:40,490 --> 00:17:41,580
Well...

235
00:17:42,870 --> 00:17:44,200
It's time.

236
00:18:12,230 --> 00:18:14,530
I'm the one who deserves to be hit!

237
00:18:14,990 --> 00:18:18,660
I'm a scoundrel, a coward,

238
00:18:19,820 --> 00:18:22,910
spineless and weak...

239
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:26,290
Don't give us any more trouble.

240
00:18:33,250 --> 00:18:39,010
<i>Eva Unit 01 will be entering Stage 2
cryo-stasis for activation system rewrite.</i>

241
00:18:39,010 --> 00:18:40,140
He's gone.

242
00:18:43,890 --> 00:18:45,600
Was it for the best?

243
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:48,270
The "Hedgehog's Dilemma".

244
00:18:49,310 --> 00:18:52,400
The closer we become,
the more deeply we hurt each other.

245
00:18:53,070 --> 00:18:54,900
Now I understand.

246
00:18:56,990 --> 00:18:58,400
That boy...

247
00:18:59,450 --> 00:19:03,660
He can't let others know how he feels
in any other way.

248
00:19:04,830 --> 00:19:09,750
<i>The Express Linear Train bound
for Atsugi is arriving on Track 2.</i>

249
00:19:09,750 --> 00:19:13,840
<i>For your safety, please step back
to the area inside the yellow lines.</i>

250
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:18,050
<i>The train arriving on Track 2 is for
special government use only</i>

251
00:19:18,050 --> 00:19:21,180
<i>and departs at 4:20 for Atsugi.</i>

252
00:19:21,180 --> 00:19:24,430
<i>No civilians are allowed inside the fence.</i>

253
00:19:24,430 --> 00:19:26,350
<i>Please be aware that the
boarding of this train</i>

254
00:19:26,350 --> 00:19:29,890
<i>by unauthorized persons
is strictly prohibited.</i>

255
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:42,660
Hang in there.

256
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:18,570
Look!

257
00:20:18,570 --> 00:20:20,990
It's that babe!

258
00:21:14,540 --> 00:21:18,880
<i>The local train bound for Gora
is now arriving on Track 4.</i>

259
00:21:19,250 --> 00:21:23,470
<i>For your own safety, please stay
inside the yellow lines.</i>

260
00:21:24,010 --> 00:21:26,180
<i>If you're accompanying small children,</i>

261
00:21:26,180 --> 00:21:28,090
<i>please ensure that they are
properly supervised.</i>

262
00:21:29,510 --> 00:21:35,440
<i>The train arriving on Track 4 is the
local shuttle to Gora departing at 4:32.</i>

263
00:21:35,810 --> 00:21:39,520
<i>If this is your train, please step inside
and wait until departure.</i>

264
00:21:40,230 --> 00:21:45,400
<i>The train is now approaching.
Please stay behind the yellow line.</i>

265
00:21:49,410 --> 00:21:51,580
I... I'm home.

266
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:57,580
Welcome home.

267
00:21:57,620 --> 00:22:00,590
TO BE CONTINUED

268
00:23:06,070 --> 00:23:07,030
PREVIEW

269
00:23:06,820 --> 00:23:10,660
Rei Ayanami limits her association
with others as much as possible.

270
00:23:10,660 --> 00:23:13,870
The only one she opens up to
is Commander lkari.

271
00:23:13,870 --> 00:23:17,160
Shinji is at a loss to understand this girl,
who is closer to his own father than he is.

272
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:20,170
Next Evangelion: "Rei, Beyond the Heart"

273
00:23:18,410 --> 00:23:21,080
REI, BEYOND THE HEART
